For each transaction, state whether it is an injection into, a withdrawal from, or neither (part of the inner flow between households and firms in) the country's circular flow of income:
(1) a textile firm in Lahore buys new weaving machines made in Pakistan;
(2) a household puts part of its income into a savings account;
(3) a tourist from Saudi Arabia pays for a hotel in Islamabad;
(4) a firm pays sales tax to the government;
(5) a household buys furniture made in Chiniot.

For each transaction, state the section of Pakistan's current account in which it is recorded and whether it is a credit or a debit:
(1) rice exported to Kenya;
(2) a Pakistani family's holiday in Turkey;
(3) interest paid by the Pakistani government on loans from foreign banks;
(4) money sent home by a Pakistani nurse working in Saudi Arabia.
